let a hud over the shell go, and keep it off the rest of the frame

On a GBA cart the volume HUD stayed on the panel, faint, after it had
faded, and the frame stayed expensive with it. The display list there is
the game, the Advance shell, then the HUD. 0032 took all of that past the
game as the overlay, shell included, so every frame the bar showed was
composed over the whole canvas -- the canvas path again. When the HUD
went, the list was the game and the shell, which takes the shell into the
surround and returned before the overlay was cleared: the HUD's last,
nearly transparent frame and the full-canvas shell went on being composed
on every frame after it, for as long as the cart ran.

With blue light on, 0032 sent any HUD through the canvas, because the
overlay was copied out ungraded. Traced on the Flip with Pokemon Emerald
on gpSP at blue light 5: 7.8 ms a frame without the HUD, 20-24 ms with it
(the game into the canvas, the 752x560 shell as a 7.7 ms sprite, a graded
copy of the whole panel), and 675 presents over 25 ms, none of them with
any overlay time.

Now:
- the shell goes into the surround whenever it is seated, and only what
  follows it is the overlay, so a GBA HUD is the 752x41 plate alone;
- the overlay is cleared on that path too;
- the overlay is graded as it is composed -- the game's rows through the
  same column mask the panel pass uses, the sprites tinted by the gain --
  so blue light keeps the direct path. A gain is a per-channel scale, so
  blending warmed sprites over warmed pixels is the canvas path's graded
  copy, give or take rounding;
- the rect an overlay covered is redrawn from the surround and the game on
  each page for PAGES frames after it changes or goes, since the direct
  pass writes only the game's rect and a HUD over the surround would
  otherwise stay there;
- an overlay that has not changed and lies off the picture is not composed
  again once every page has it. One over the picture still is, every frame,
  as the game pass has just written over it.

Tests: a HUD over the shell leaves the shell out of the overlay; frames
after a HUD has gone match, pixel for pixel, frames that never had one,
upright and mirrored; a still HUD off the picture is not composed again;
with blue light at its warmest a HUD over the shell stays direct and lands
within 2 of the cold frame through the gain table, upright and mirrored.
The first three fail without this patch; run as armv7 under qemu with
`task test`.

Applies on top of 0033, upstream 91499a9.

